<section image-layout="blank" id="aRGt5c88w5"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="ZhJiyO8TJT" background-color="palette-3" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><p role="eyebrow">Humanitarian reading</p><h2>Dignity under pressure</h2><p font-size="18pt"><b>Constrained choice is not the same as moral failure.</b></p><p font-size="18pt">The poem asks not only what happens to Kiều, but what kind of world makes her sacrifices necessary.</p></grid-item><grid-item vertical-align="center" colspan="40"><h3>Episode → action → interpretation</h3><table borders="rows" striped="false" col-widths="[18,22,20]"><tr><th>Episode</th><th>What Kiều does</th><th background-color="surface">Humanitarian insight</th></tr><tr><td><b>Family crisis</b></td><td>Sells herself to protect her family.</td><td background-color="surface">The sacrifice is admirable; the demand is unjust.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Mã Giám Sinh and Tú Bà</b></td><td>Tries to survive sale and coercion.</td><td background-color="surface">Constraint must not be confused with moral failure.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Từ Hải</b></td><td>Acts within a brief reversal of power.</td><td background-color="surface">Talent and judgment emerge when shelter exists.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Giác Duyên and reunion</b></td><td>Survives and renegotiates return.</td><td background-color="surface">Rescue matters; accumulated harm is not cancelled.</td></tr></table><p font-size="12pt">Episode reference: <a href="https://www.nomfoundation.org/nom-project/Tale-of-Kieu?uiLang=vn"><i>Tale of Kiều</i>, Vietnamese Nôm Preservation Foundation</a>. Interpretations are identified as readings, not direct quotations.</p></grid-item></grid></section>